# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. Never commit real secrets.
#
# This file is the SINGLE place for keys and service endpoints:
#   - the Python clients read it directly (loaded on demand, process env wins);
#   - `python scripts/gen_mcp_json.py` renders the in-session MCP registration
#     (.mcp.json, also gitignored) from it — rerun that after editing this file.
# Lookup order for `.env`: $SV_HOME/.env, then ./.env (current directory), then the
# repo root when running from a git checkout. The first file that sets a key wins.
# SV_HOME=/abs/path/to/your/workspace

# --- LLM (required for real-LLM runs; no-token runs with llm_kind "scripted" need none) ---
# Put your key after the "=". While it is empty, runs that call an LLM fail (the from-scratch
# studies, scripts/demo_offline.py and the Chicago adapter fall back to OPENAI_API_KEY).
SV_LLM_API_KEY=
# Optional; leave commented to keep the defaults. Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (unset: the
# official OpenAI API):
# SV_LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# Model name, read by scripts/demo_offline.py (in place of the study's model), the Chicago
# adapter, and studies whose simulation.json decision_args name no model. The shipped
# from-scratch studies pin decision_args.model in simulation.json (consumer_confidence:
# prediction.model in environment.json), so on another endpoint change it there, or through
# /sv-iterate for a study that has already run.
# SV_LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-2024-08-06

# --- Companion repos (only for the studies that wrap them; tests SKIP when absent) ---
# Recommended layout: clone them as SIBLINGS of this repo and set nothing here, e.g.
#   git clone https://github.com/Lishi905/SocioVerse-ABM ../SocioVerse-ABM
#   git clone https://github.com/RunRiotComeOn/ConsumerSim-Consumer-Confidence-Forecast \
#       ../ConsumerSim-Consumer-Confidence-Forecast
#   git clone https://github.com/xymou/HiSim ../HiSim
# Overrides for other layouts:
# SocioVerse-ABM repo ROOT (the dir holding socioverse_abm/ and tasks/): the 11 abm_* studies,
# and the default place chicago_schelling looks for the legacy Chicago model.
# SV_ABM_ROOT=/abs/path/to/SocioVerse-ABM
# The legacy Chicago model dir ITSELF (holds src/, config/, processed_data/); only needed when
# it is not at $SV_ABM_ROOT/tasks/organization/chicago_segregation/legacy.
# SV_CHICAGO_LEGACY=/abs/path/to/SocioVerse-ABM/tasks/organization/chicago_segregation/legacy
# ConsumerSim checkout (consumer_confidence study):
# SV_CONSUMERSIM_ROOT=/abs/path/to/ConsumerSim-Consumer-Confidence-Forecast
# HiSim checkout with its data/ (only the hisim_roe real-data tests use it):
# SV_HISIM_ROOT=/abs/path/to/HiSim

# --- Optional data services ---
# The event and user-pool data services are optional and currently hosted by the SocioVerse
# team; to request access, email contact@socioverse.fudan-disc.com. Without them the skills
# fall back to web search and synthesized personas (see resources/capabilities.yaml).
#
# External events service (Event MCP; used at BUILD time by sv-build-environment, never by
# the runtime loop — see socioverse/external_events.py for the fallback chain).
# URL is the FULL MCP endpoint (streamable HTTP); the key is sent as Authorization: Bearer.
# SV_EVENT_API_URL=https://your-event-host/event_mcp
# SV_EVENT_API_KEY=your-event-mcp-key
# Optional offline fallback: a dir of <source>/<YYYY-MM>.json cached payloads
# SV_EVENT_LOCAL_CACHE=/abs/path/to/event-cache
#
# User-pool survey MCP (platform personas + questionnaire answering for P); used at BUILD
# time via the in-session MCP tools (sv-build-population / sv-report), registered into
# .mcp.json by scripts/gen_mcp_json.py.
# The key is sent as Authorization: Bearer (the service requires it).
# SV_USER_POOL_MCP_URL=https://your-pool-host/user_pool_mcp
# SV_USER_POOL_MCP_KEY=your-pool-key

# --- Dashboard (optional) ---
# These are NOT read from this file: dashboard/hooks/sv_emit.py runs inside the Claude Code
# session and reads its environment. Export them in the shell you launch Claude Code from, or
# put them under "env" in .claude/settings.local.json. Full list: dashboard/README.md.
#   SV_DASH_PYTHON=/abs/path/to/venv/bin/python  # python that runs the server; needs duckdb for
#                                                # the data tables (default: the hook's python)
#   SV_DASH_PORT=8787                            # use a different port per checkout
#   SV_DASH_OPEN=0                               # don't open a browser tab (URL still printed)
#   SV_DASH_DISABLE=1                            # never start, announce or contact the dashboard
#   SV_DASH_IDLE=1800                            # idle self-shutdown in seconds (default: off)
